# ============================================================
# Notes & disabled keys (preserved verbatim from the original)
# ============================================================
# Inner G Complete Agency — Client Intelligence Portal
# Environment Variables Reference
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your values.
# NEVER commit .env.local to git (it is in .gitignore).
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED — Core Supabase (always needed)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Your Supabase project URL
# Found at: Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API
# Your Supabase anon/public key (safe to expose in browser)
# Found at: Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED — Production site URL
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SERVER-ONLY — Never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_
# These are NEVER bundled in browser JavaScript.
# Set these in Vercel Dashboard → Project → Environment Variables (for Next.js)
# and in Supabase Dashboard → Edge Functions → Secrets (for Edge Functions)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Supabase service role key — bypasses ALL RLS policies.
# Use ONLY in server-side code and Edge Functions.
# Google Gemini API Key
# Get from: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# Google Maps / Places API Key — used for Places (New) ingestion scripts
# (shops, barbers, supply stores). Get from: https://console.cloud.google.com/google/maps-apis
# GoHighLevel API Key — Inner G's internal agency account
# Get from: GHL Dashboard → Settings → Business Profile → API Keys
# GoHighLevel Location ID — Inner G's agency sub-account location
# GoHighLevel Webhook Secret — for verifying inbound webhook signatures
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PER-CLIENT (added on demand when a client integration is built)
# These follow the pattern: CLIENT_SLUG_VARIABLE_NAME
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Example: Kane's Bookstore Instagram API
# KANES_INSTAGRAM_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# KANES_INSTAGRAM_ACCOUNT_ID=
# Example: Plenty of Hearts TikTok API
# POH_TIKTOK_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# POH_TIKTOK_REFRESH_TOKEN=
# POH_TIKTOK_OPEN_ID=
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BOOKSY AGENT (scripts/booksy-agent/agent.js)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# --- Gemini: the chat feature has its own key, on its own Cloud project ---
#
# Google rate-limits PER PROJECT, not per key. GEMINI_API_KEY is shared with
# ~25 batch scripts and ~15 edge functions, so a backfill run from a laptop
# used to draw down the same allowance as live chat — and a staging test drew
# down production's. GEMINI_CHAT_API_KEY separates them.
#
#   Vercel Production  -> key from the ShearQuery-Production Cloud project
#   Vercel Preview     -> key from the ShearQuery-Development Cloud project
#   .env.local         -> key from the ShearQuery-Development Cloud project
#
# MUST be added to Production and Preview as two SEPARATE Vercel entries, each
# scoped to one environment. A single entry targeting both is one shared value,
# which is the exact problem this variable exists to fix.
#
# If unset, chat falls back to GEMINI_API_KEY and logs a warning saying it is
# not isolated. It will work; it just won't be separated.

# Shared secret that lets a trusted server-side agent call /api/chat as a known
# member without a session cookie. Used by the Instagram DM agent, whose caller
# is a Meta webhook and which resolves identity from a sender id rather than a
# browser.
#
# Absent = closed, never open-by-default: without it /api/chat ignores the
# memberId in the body entirely and every DM is answered anonymously. That is a
# safe degradation, but it silently removes the whole point of linking an
# account, so set it wherever the DM agent runs.
# INTERNAL_AGENT_SECRET=
